  "id": "macroelectrode",
  "term": "macroelectrode",
  "definition": "A macroelectrode is the chronic electrode used in deep brain stimulation after the intraoperative microelectrode is removed. Compared with a microelectrode, its larger geometry mainly changes the strength of stimulation effects rather than their overall pattern, although differences in placement can produce different stimulation of nearby nerve fibers.",
